    },
    "message": "Read a hyphenated facility ID as a target, not a negative count\n\nThe offline parser's count pattern accepted a sign right after the facility\ntoken, so \"toilet-1を故障させる\" became a request to stop -1 units. It was\nrejected with a message about the evacuee count, because the invalid-count\nnoun fell through to 避難者 for every operation except staff and toilets.\n\nA sign now counts only when no letter or digit is glued to it, so\n\"staff -2\" is still rejected as an invalid count. A facility outage names\nthe stopped units in its message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
